          {
            "title": "Question: One value",
            "id": 88623,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Por que esta lista tem dois elementos?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"water = [(\" /><text value=\"&quot;hydrogen&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"11.19\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"), (\" /><text value=\"&quot;oxygen&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"88.81\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(len(water))\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"2\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Porque cada tupla conta como um elemento</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Porque cada tupla tem dois tipos de valores</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Porque cada tupla conta como um elemento.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A lista contém quatro valores no total. Por que <code>len(water)</code> exibe <code>2</code>?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"water = [(\" /><text value=\"&quot;hydrogen&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"11.19\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"), (\" /><text value=\"&quot;oxygen&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"88.81\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\")]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(len(water))\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"2\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Porque <code>len()</code> conta as tuplas, não os valores dentro delas.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Porque <code>len()</code> conta apenas os nomes, não os números.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Porque <code>len()</code> conta quantos valores cada tupla contém.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Porque <code>len()</code> conta as tuplas, não os valores dentro delas.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
