        "id": 9914,
        "title": "Tuplas vs listas",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Intro",
            "id": 88368,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Vamos observar as semelhanças e diferenças entre tuplas como <code>event_tuple</code> e listas como <code>days_list</code>, para saber quando usar uma ou outra.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"event_tuple = (\" /><text value=\"&quot;Saturday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;21:00&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Anna's Bday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"days_list = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Saturday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sunday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /></content></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Access by index",
            "id": 88369,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>De forma semelhante às listas, podemos acessar os valores de uma tupla pelo seu índice, como aqui com <code>event_tuple[1]</code> para obter o horário.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"event_tuple = (\" /><text value=\"&quot;Saturday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;21:00&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Anna's Bday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(event_tuple[\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"57\" endIndex=\"71\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"21:00\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>event_tuple[1]</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Immutable 1",
            "id": 88370,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A principal diferença é que, ao contrário das listas, <em>não podemos</em> atualizar, adicionar ou excluir valores de tuples.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"event_tuple = (\" /><text value=\"&quot;Saturday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;21:00&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Anna's Bday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"days_list = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Saturday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sunday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"days_list[\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"] = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Friday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Immutable 2",
            "id": 88371,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Dizemos que as tuplas são imutáveis, pois tentar modificá-las como aqui com <code>event_tuple[0] = \"Friday\"</code> resulta em um erro.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"event_tuple = (\" /><text value=\"&quot;Saturday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;21:00&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Anna's Bday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"event_tuple[\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"] = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Friday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"51\" endIndex=\"65\" /><option startIndex=\"66\" endIndex=\"67\" /><option startIndex=\"68\" endIndex=\"76\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Traceback (most recent call last):\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  File &quot;file.py&quot;, line 2, in &lt;module&gt;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    event_tuple[0] = &quot;Friday&quot;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"TypeError: 'tuple' object does not support item assignment\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>event_tuple[0]</code> seguido de <code>=</code> e finalmente <code>\"Friday\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Tuplas são <strong>imutáveis</strong>: seus valores não mudam. Substitua o primeiro por <code>\"Friday\"</code> para gerar um erro.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"event_tuple = (\" /><text value=\"&quot;Saturday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;21:00&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Anna's Bday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"event_tuple[\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"] = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Friday&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"51\" endIndex=\"65\" /><option startIndex=\"66\" endIndex=\"67\" /><option startIndex=\"68\" endIndex=\"76\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"event_tuple\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"event_tuple[1]\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Traceback (most recent call last):\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  File &quot;file.py&quot;, line 2, in &lt;module&gt;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    event_tuple[0] = &quot;Friday&quot;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"TypeError: 'tuple' object does not support item assignment\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>event_tuple[0]</code> seguido de <code>=</code> e finalmente <code>\"Friday\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Immutable 3",
            "id": 88372,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Como as tuples são imutáveis, nós as usamos para armazenar informações que não devem ser modificadas, como o nome e a data de nascimento de uma pessoa.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"personal_data = (\" /><text value=\"&quot;Anna&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;21.05&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option startIndex=\"32\" endIndex=\"33\" /><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"32\" /><option startIndex=\"23\" endIndex=\"24\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>(</code> seguido de <code>,</code> e depois <code>\"21.05\"</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Como as tuples são imutáveis, nós as usamos para armazenar informações que não devem ser modificadas, como o nome e a data de nascimento de uma pessoa.</p><p>Armazene <code>\"Anna\"</code> e sua data de nascimento <code>\"21.05\"</code> em uma tupla.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"personal_data = (\" /><text value=\"&quot;Anna&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;21.05&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option startIndex=\"23\" endIndex=\"24\" /><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"32\" /><option startIndex=\"32\" endIndex=\"33\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"[\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"]\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>(</code> seguido de <code>,</code>, <code>\"21.05\"</code> e finalmente <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
